# Plan of flight — SPEC-004

## Plan mode

Origin: planned; reconstruction: false; revision: 1. Recommended mode: per-plan. No execution checkpoint has been approved or activated.

## Recommended approach

Fix the upstream contract and adoption guidance before creating visual specialist packages. Reuse existing state fields and policies, add semantic checks and scenario evidence, and promote the exact supplemental DEC-002 only within explicit approval.

## Reuse

DEC-001, game discovery, existing approval contract, state schema, plan/templates and dependency-free local Node runtime. No new dependency, framework or agent runtime.

## Implementation sequence

1. `S-001` — Recheck scope/state; record selected mode/checkpoint and approved DEC-002 promotion; activate cursor.
2. `S-002` — Define applicable visual readiness and adoption/bootstrap guidance; update game and instruction templates.
3. `S-003` — Implement progress, next-step preparation, draft/canon notices and configuration defaults while preserving approval modes.
4. `S-004` — Add read-only semantic state validation and fixtures covering supported modes and invalid combinations/references.
5. `S-005` — Verify criteria, scenario decisions, templates, IDs/links/state and diff; repair within limits.
6. `S-006` — Record results, promotion/status evidence and deferred migration/package work; reconcile and clear cursor.

## Approval checkpoints

Recommended per-plan: PLAN covers S-001 through S-006, including the exact DEC-002 promotion. Alternative per-batch: B-001 covers S-001–S-003; B-002 covers S-004–S-006. Alternative per-step: each S-XXX is its own checkpoint. Select and record the route before execution; never inherit SPEC-003 approval.

## Expected changes

Seventeen upstream files and bounded operational records listed in [spec.md](spec.md), plus DEC-002 after approval. No edits to local games/global instructions or the state schema.

## Validation

- All acceptance criteria checked against actual files and representative scenarios.
- Semantic fixtures: known plan/spec/step, active cursor, mode/checkpoint match, approved/pending boundary, suspension, duplicate deferred IDs and truthful idle state.
- PENDING is valid paused persistence; readiness-to-execute must be false. Schema validity is not execution permission.
- Test progress counts with nonconsecutive stable step IDs and revised plan totals; next-step preparation never grants an unapproved checkpoint.
- Demonstrate no visual specialist execution when required baseline is missing; document actual review as documentary/simulated unless a model is separately run.
- Resolve local links, metadata/IDs, required paths and default configuration consistency; validate closed idle state against existing schema.

## Limits

Seventeen upstream files, approved DEC-002 and operational records. Maximum three repair attempts per failing check. No installs, live delegation/model runs, game execution, publication or other-project mutation.

## Recovery

Preserve existing file versions before implementation; revert only this run's changes with reviewable patches. Preserve unrelated drafts and local project rules. If stopped, record partial outcome before clearing the activated cursor; never falsify approval or promotion history.

## Mandatory gates

Guided ADD checkpoint approval covers the proposed process edits and specifically identified canonical promotion. Other-project migration, global configuration, new dependencies, sensitive remote context, asset production and publication need separate scope/authority.

